# K1000 Wi-Fi access point, hostapd backend: the default (setup-ap.sh; docs/06-phone.md §1, §6).
# NetworkManager's AP mode (wpa_supplicant, `--backend nm`) does not carry phones on the Pi's
# onboard Broadcom chip: the hub's knowledge drawer rpi-internal-wifi-ap-hostapd (clients
# associate, then get no DHCP and are dropped after ~6 s; hostapd + PMF off is what worked).
# NetworkManager leaves the interface alone (conf.d/k1000-ap-unmanaged.conf, setup-ap.sh).
#
# - Never unfenced: Requires= the fence (stopping it stops the AP), and the first ExecStartPre
#   refuses to start when its nftables table is not loaded (a fence skipped by its condition, or
#   flushed by hand, is not a failed unit: Requires= alone would not see it).
# - Never in an occupied subnet: the second ExecStartPre refuses while another interface holds an
#   address in the AP's subnet (a laptop on eth0 with NetworkManager's "Shared to other
#   computers", 10.42.0.1/24 too: the AP would make the laptop's address local to the box and SSH
#   over eth0 would be lost). It leaves /run/k1000-ap-guard.stopped, so the NetworkManager guard
#   (90-k1000-ap-guard) starts the AP once that address is gone.
# - Bound to its interface by the drop-in k1000-ap-hostapd.service.d/k1000-iface.conf (setup-ap.sh:
#   BindsTo= + After= the interface's device): no start before it exists, a stop when it goes.
# - A finite start limit: a hostapd that keeps dying (a refused channel, a driver error) or a
#   refused start stops being retried after 8 starts in 2 min; setup-ap.sh resets it.
# - Interface and address come from /etc/k1000/ap.env (setup-ap.sh).
# - The Wi-Fi radio is unblocked through sysfs (no rfkill binary needed).
# - Any address left on the interface is flushed first: NetworkManager's carries noprefixroute and
#   `ip addr replace` never rewrites it, which would leave the AP subnet without a route. The AP
#   address is then set while the link is down; hostapd brings it up.
# - hostapd.conf (0600: it holds the password) leaves ieee80211w unset: PMF off.
[Unit]
Description=K1000 Wi-Fi access point (hostapd)
Documentation=file:///opt/k1000/net/setup-ap.sh
Requires=k1000-ap-fence.service
Wants=network-pre.target k1000-ap-dnsmasq.service
After=network-pre.target k1000-ap-fence.service NetworkManager.service
StartLimitIntervalSec=120
StartLimitBurst=8

[Service]
Type=simple
EnvironmentFile=/etc/k1000/ap.env
ExecStartPre=/bin/sh -c '/usr/sbin/nft list table inet k1000_ap >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "k1000-ap: REFUSED: the fence (nftables table inet k1000_ap) is not loaded: the AP never runs unfenced" >&2; exit 1; }'
ExecStartPre=/bin/sh -c '/usr/sbin/ip -4 -o addr show to "$$K1000_AP_ADDR" | while read -r n dev fam addr rest; do [ "$$dev" = "$$K1000_AP_IFACE" ] || { : > /run/k1000-ap-guard.stopped; echo "k1000-ap: REFUSED: $$dev holds $$addr, inside the AP subnet $$K1000_AP_ADDR (a laptop on eth0 sharing its connection?): the AP stays down so eth0 keeps working" >&2; exit 1; }; done'
ExecStartPre=/bin/sh -c 'for r in /sys/class/rfkill/rfkill*; do [ "$$(cat "$$r/type" 2>/dev/null)" = wlan ] && echo 0 > "$$r/soft"; done; exit 0'
ExecStartPre=/usr/sbin/ip addr flush dev ${K1000_AP_IFACE}
ExecStartPre=/usr/sbin/ip link set ${K1000_AP_IFACE} down
ExecStartPre=/usr/sbin/ip addr add ${K1000_AP_ADDR} dev ${K1000_AP_IFACE}
ExecStart=/usr/sbin/hostapd /etc/k1000/hostapd.conf
ExecStopPost=-/usr/sbin/ip addr flush dev ${K1000_AP_IFACE}
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=3

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
